1
00:00:00,088 --> 00:00:03,762
Native Foundation is a separate planning and controlled-adapter lane.

2
00:00:04,175 --> 00:00:08,362
Do not confuse it with the classic Foundation V M deployment workflow

3
00:00:08,775 --> 00:00:10,412
used elsewhere in this series.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:15,475
Inspect its returned read-only state, adapter readiness and blockers.

5
00:00:15,862 --> 00:00:20,425
A long list of successful review artifacts does not mean that physical

6
00:00:20,475 --> 00:00:23,075
imaging or cluster formation has taken place.

7
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:28,779
A hardware probe can test selected connectivity and authentication

8
00:00:28,779 --> 00:00:29,454
conditions.

9
00:00:29,854 --> 00:00:31,842
Read each result and its scope.

10
00:00:32,242 --> 00:00:35,804
A passed count can represent checks rather than the number of configured

11
00:00:35,804 --> 00:00:36,367
nodes.

12
00:00:36,742 --> 00:00:41,642
Review manifests, provider operations, missing evidence and enabled

13
00:00:41,729 --> 00:00:43,454
execution flags separately.

14
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:48,492
Evidence records, reservation plans and authorization reviews do not

15
00:00:48,492 --> 00:00:51,817
themselves prove that a deployment was admitted or executed.

16
00:00:53,017 --> 00:00:57,079
The post-foundation baseline workflows classify controls as apply,

17
00:00:57,542 --> 00:00:59,667
evidence, manual or blocked.

18
00:01:00,067 --> 00:01:02,567
Only verified apply mappings execute.

19
00:01:02,942 --> 00:01:05,917
Evidence-only records capture observations.

20
00:01:06,317 --> 00:01:10,804
Manual controls still require a supported target procedure and retained

21
00:01:10,804 --> 00:01:11,292
proof.

22
00:01:11,704 --> 00:01:14,029
Blocked controls need their gate resolved.

23
00:01:14,429 --> 00:01:19,117
A successful overall job does not mean that every requested security,

24
00:01:19,504 --> 00:01:22,917
monitoring, network or certificate setting was changed.

25
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:28,088
For hardware out-of-band access, controller credentials and certificates,

26
00:01:28,288 --> 00:01:31,762
confirm the supported platform procedure and your recovery path.

27
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:35,975
Inspect any manual follow-up rather than treating an acknowledgement

28
00:01:36,175 --> 00:01:36,988
as completion.

29
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:40,875
Review independent target evidence for the controls that matter.

30
00:01:41,288 --> 00:01:43,712
Reconcile partial changes before retry.

31
00:01:44,112 --> 00:01:48,050
Keep both the configuration intent and the actual verified result

32
00:01:48,062 --> 00:01:48,938
with the change record.

33
00:01:50,142 --> 00:01:54,792
Before enabling a specialist integration, verify its exact supported

34
00:01:54,792 --> 00:01:58,979
scope, keep approvals and preserve the original recovery path.

35
00:01:59,392 --> 00:02:03,817
Use the established Foundation V M and post-configuration workflows

36
00:02:03,892 --> 00:02:05,392
for the core cluster tasks.

37
00:02:05,804 --> 00:02:08,742
Check actual target state before accepting a change.

38
00:02:09,142 --> 00:02:11,967
Open Overview when you are ready to choose your next task.
